{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "rows": [
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-eq-namespace",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member == namespace",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } },
        { "name": "namespace", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "display": "Color" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The critical row. Both operands are ObjectRepr::Map with Enumerator::NonEnumerable, and the member's value_cmp declines against the namespace, so the engine reaches the map arm. `a.try_iter_pairs()` is None, so equality is FALSE (value/mod.rs:545-552). Treating both as empty key slices made it true."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/namespace-eq-member",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "namespace == member",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } },
        { "name": "namespace", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "display": "Color" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The same pair with the operands swapped. The left side still cannot be enumerated, so this is false too."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-ne-namespace",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member != namespace",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } },
        { "name": "namespace", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "display": "Color" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The negated spelling, which is what a template guard actually writes."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/namespace-ne-member",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "namespace != member",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } },
        { "name": "namespace", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "display": "Color" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "And negated from the other operand position."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/namespace-eq-other-namespace",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "namespace == other",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "namespace", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "display": "Color" } },
        { "name": "other", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "display": "Shade" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "Two opaque maps with no comparison hook at all: neither declines into an answer, and the map arm still says false."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-in-namespace-seq",
      "surface": "container",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member in [namespace]",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } },
        { "name": "namespace", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "display": "Color" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "Sequence membership tests `item == needle`, so the CONTAINER's item is the left operand. This is the orientation an `in` guard reaches."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/namespace-in-member-seq",
      "surface": "container",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "namespace in [member]",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } },
        { "name": "namespace", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "display": "Color" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The other membership orientation."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-in-two-namespaces",
      "surface": "container",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member in [namespace, other]",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } },
        { "name": "namespace", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "display": "Color" } },
        { "name": "other", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "display": "Shade" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "More than one candidate, so a false answer is not an artefact of a one-element sequence."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-eq-empty-map",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member == {}",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "A non-enumerable LEFT map against a known-empty right one: false, because the left has no pair iterator."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/empty-map-eq-member",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "{} == member",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The deliberate asymmetry, and stock authority: a KNOWN-EMPTY left map reaches the length fallback, where a non-enumerable right side counts as zero, so this is TRUE where the reversed spelling is false (value/mod.rs:554-558)."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-ne-empty-map",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member != {}",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The negated spelling of the same asymmetry."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/empty-map-ne-member",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "{} != member",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "And from the other side."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-in-empty-map-seq",
      "surface": "container",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member in [{}]",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "Membership makes the asymmetry visible: the item `{}` is on the left, so this asks `{} == member` and is TRUE. Adding a membership shortcut, or comparing the needle from the other side, would flip it."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/empty-map-in-member-seq",
      "surface": "container",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "{} in [member]",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The reverse orientation of the same pair, which is false. The two rows together are what pin the orientation itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/nonempty-map-eq-member",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "{'a': 'b'} == member",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The length fallback is a comparison against ZERO, not a blanket truth: a non-empty enumerable left map is still unequal to an opaque one."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-eq-nonempty-map",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member == {'a': 'b'}",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "And the same pair reversed."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-eq-same-canonical",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member == twin",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } },
        { "name": "twin", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "red" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The map fallback must stay a LAST resort. Two members with the same canonical value are equal through the comparison hook, even though they display differently and neither enumerates."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-eq-other-member",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member == blue",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } },
        { "name": "blue", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "BLUE", "display": "bleu" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "Two members with different canonical values: the hook answers, and it answers unequal."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-eq-canonical-string",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member == 'RED'",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The hook still runs before the kind rules, so a member compares equal to its canonical string rather than to what it displays."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/string-eq-member",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "'RED' == member",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The hook from the RIGHT operand position, which is the commutativity half of the dispatch."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-lt-namespace",
      "surface": "comparison",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member < namespace",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } },
        { "name": "namespace", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "display": "Color" } }
      ],
      "expect": "bytes",
      "notes": "Ordering two map operands needs a pair iterator from BOTH, and the engine has no arm for a missing one: `match (a.try_iter_pairs(), b.try_iter_pairs()) { (Some, Some) => .., _ => unreachable!() }` (value/mod.rs:653-661). Both sides must FAULT. Returning an ordering, a decline or a false would each be a stronger answer than the engine's."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/namespace-lt-member",
      "surface": "comparison",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "namespace < member",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } },
        { "name": "namespace", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "display": "Color" } }
      ],
      "expect": "bytes",
      "notes": "The same fault from the other operand position. The member's hook is tried from the right and declines, so ordering still reaches the map arm."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-lt-empty-map",
      "surface": "comparison",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member < {}",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "bytes",
      "notes": "One enumerable operand is not enough: `unreachable!()` needs only ONE missing pair iterator."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/empty-map-lt-member",
      "surface": "comparison",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "{} < member",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "bytes",
      "notes": "And with the enumerable operand on the left, which is the case a length-based ordering would have answered 0 for."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-lt-canonical-string",
      "surface": "comparison",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member < 'S'",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The control for the fault rows: when the comparison hook DOES answer, ordering succeeds normally and nothing faults. 'RED' < 'S'."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-lt-other-member",
      "surface": "comparison",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "blue < member",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } },
        { "name": "blue", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "BLUE", "display": "bleu" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "Two members order by canonical value through the hook, so the fault never applies to the pair a template most often orders."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/empty-map-lt-nonempty-map",
      "surface": "comparison",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "{} < {'a': 'b'}",
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "The ordinary-mapping control: two enumerable maps still order structurally, so the fault cannot have swallowed the normal path."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-is-mapping",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member is mapping",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "Representation and enumerability are separate questions: the object IS a mapping, which is exactly why it takes the map arm of equality and ordering."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-is-iterable",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member is iterable",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "boolean",
      "notes": "...and it is NOT iterable, which is the other half of the same fact."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-truthy",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
      "form": "template",
      "source": "{% if member %}T{% else %}F{% endif %}",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "bytes",
      "notes": "Truthiness is `enumerator_len() != Some(0)`, and an unknown length is not Some(0), so an opaque map is TRUE where `{}` is false. A third fact that a keys-are-empty model got wrong."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/empty-map-falsey",
      "surface": "value_cmp",
