        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "error",
      "notes": "An opaque map is not silently an empty iterable: iterating it is an error, not zero passes through the loop body."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-list",
      "surface": "container",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member|list",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "error",
      "notes": "`try_iter` is the object's `enumerate()`, not its `repr()` (value/object.rs:361-379). Every iterating filter asks the same question the loop does, so `|list` errors rather than answering `[]`."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-join",
      "surface": "container",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member|join(\",\")",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "error",
      "notes": "The same through a filter that walks its subject to build a string, where an empty answer would silently render nothing."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-first",
      "surface": "container",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member|first",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "error",
      "notes": "`first` is `as_object().and_then(|x| x.try_iter())` (filters.rs:686-697): a missing iterator is the error arm, not an undefined result."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-reverse",
      "surface": "container",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member|reverse",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "error",
      "notes": "`Value::reverse` branches on the enumerator and its first arm is `Enumerator::NonEnumerable => None` (value/mod.rs:1411), so reversing an opaque map is `cannot reverse values of type map`."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-items",
      "surface": "container",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member|items",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "bytes",
      "notes": "`items` is the one that does NOT fail: it gates on the KIND and then yields a single invalid value from inside the iterable (filters.rs:363-377), which is the engine's error-as-a-value repr. The distinction only exists because the two questions are asked in different places."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-length",
      "surface": "container",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member|length",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "error",
