      "surface": "rendering",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "debug(member)",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "bytes",
      "notes": "`debug(x)` is `format!(\"{x:#?}\")`, so the alternate debug layout is chosen the same way `render` chooses it: a mapping is a `debug_map` over its PAIRS, and an object with none falls back to its own debug form. Formatting it as an empty map printed `{}` for a value the engine renders as itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-pprint",
      "surface": "rendering",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member|pprint",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "bytes",
      "notes": "`pprint` is the same formatting through a filter."
    },
    {
      "id": "opaque/member-tojson",
      "surface": "rendering",
      "form": "expression",
      "source": "member|tojson",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "member", "value": { "kind": "opaque_map", "canonical": "RED", "display": "rouge" } }
      ],
      "expect": "bytes",
      "notes": "Serialization is NOT rendering: an opaque map serializes as the empty object it has no pairs for, which is the one place `{}` is the right answer."
